{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>With the oath of the oath.</b> An oath of curse." "<b>May YHWH make you a curse.</b> That all people will curse by you — \"May it come upon you the way it came upon So-and-so.\"" "<b>And for an oath.</b> That all people will swear by you — \"If only it will not happen to me the way it happened to So-and-so.\" And so it says, ״וְהִנַּחְתֶּם שִׁמְכֶם לִשְׁבוּעָה לִבְחִירַי״ (Isaiah 65) — that the righteous swear by the punishment of the wicked. And likewise regarding blessing: ״וְנִבְרְכוּ וגו׳״ (Genesis 12), ״בְּךָ יְבָרֵךְ יִשְׂרָאֵל לֵאמֹר״ (ibid. 48)." "<b>Your thigh.</b> In the curse He placed thigh before belly, because with it she began the transgression first (Sotah 8)." "<b>To swell.</b> As the Targum renders it — swollen."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:09:34.010056036Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}